gioedema with a vapor-heated C1 inhibitor concentrate</article-title><source><italic>The New England Journal of Medicine</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>334</volume><issue>25</issue><fpage>1630</fpage><lpage>1634</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8628358</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gelfand</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Atkinson</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hereditary angioedema: the clinical syndrome and its management</article-title><source><italic>Annals of Internal Medicine</italic></source><year>1976</year><volume>84</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>580</fpage><lpage>593</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1275365</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gelfand</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherins</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Alling</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Treatment of hereditary angioedema with danazol.Reversal of clinical and biochemical abnormalities</article-title><source><italic>The New England Journal of Medicine</italic></source><year>1976</year><volume>295</volume><issue>26</issue><fpage>1444</fpage><lpage>1448</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">792688</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><table-wrap id="tab1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p> Demographic data in various group of angioedema.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th rowspan="2" colspan="1"> Characteristics </th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Angioedema total (<inline-formula><mml